[[ch03-new-democracy-introduction]]

A hidden aspect of the MAGA movement is that it is impossible for a single culture to support millions of people. Neither the left nor the right understand this. There can be no national identity. There can be no nation as an identity. Only the least tyranny of the largest sub-culture. The "glue" that holds America together, the largest sub-culture of "least" tyranny is capitalism and not Christianity as MAGA asserts. Oddly enough, this observation was made before 1776. Only then it was just called trade. Trade was the root of the revolution. The trade triangle was British goods to Africa, slaves from Africa to the Americas, and then American rum, lumber and tobacco back to Britain. The U.S. was founded on trade that eventually evolved into capitalism.

It is important to recognize that the South with plantations and slaves was a distinct culture from New England. In addition New England had many opposing factions with such groups as the Quakers of Pennsylvania. Freedom to people in that era meant cultures that were diametrically opposed were allowed to exist and not be homogenized into one culture. This is not the case today whether it is MAGA or the left. Herd immunity for vaccines is a worthy homogenization effort of culture, but it is not realistic. What we should be shooting for is distinct land areas of herd immunity. This is no different than each country having their own vaccine policies. The U.S. needs to regroup by land area with enforced cultural boundaries.

Another hidden aspect of true American exceptionalism is isolation. America is isolated in two dimensions. First the oceans on both sides and the historically long distance from Europe meant peace. The second dimension is the large land mass of the country providing built-in isolation. People were spread out. Since its beginning, America has turned into the country mouse versus city mouse childhood books I grew up with. The U.S. Census states that densely populated areas now account for 80.0% of the U.S. population. The sparsely populated  20% of U.S. population lives in 90% of the land area. This 80% population density versus 90% land area tension defines American politics, defines MAGA, and exposes one of the many outdated flaws of the U.S. Constitution. America is no longer isolated with 80% of its population living in high density urban areas. We are trying the impossible. We are trying to map a single culture onto 340 million people who are densely populated.

The history of our isolation elimination is the history of technology. As technology advanced and roads were built, suburbs were built, and so on the isolation was eliminated. Mass communication, mass transportation and eventually the information age completed the elimination of isolation. The fly-over States were unsustainable as isolated cultures.

Isolation allowed The U.S. to not be a singular American identity, a singular culture. However, the myth that the U.S. shared a singular American identity has been with us since the beginning. So, MAGA and the left are both chasing a fictional myth; a holy grail of common culture. That is not possible. Evolution doesn't work by uniformity. Our choices today are presented as destroying our culture to bring back isolation or submit to the largest culture of least tyranny: capitalism via AI.

There is another choice, however, New Democracy. New Democracy is deceptively simple in its design. There are just two components: MGOS and projects. MGO are micro-governing organizations. MGOs are fixed size 30 people representing a micro-culture where people focus 90% of their attention within the MGO. This is due to MGOs being survival units. Each MGO is required to have one year's supply of food, water, energy, etc. on hand before joining projects. They are akin to the Starship Enterprise of Star Trek; self-sufficient yet having the latest in high-tech capabilities.

MGOs are stationery starships. Call them planetary ships. MGOs are designed to be self-sufficient and while using the latest high-tech. In Star Trek, people on the Starship Enterprise primarily focus attention on day-to-day necessities of the starship. This is also how MGOs operate.

The challenge before us is to provide isolation where people can form small cultures of understandable scope yet integrate tightly to expand high-tech optimally. To this end the fir component, MGOs, manage culture where the second component, projects, manage high-tech.

I have just described a mesh. The mesh is made up of mesh nodes, MGOs, connected by a network, projects.

The first question I typically get when introducing New Democracy is about the justified fear of tribalism violence.

First, New Democracy is anti-Utopia, anti-uniform culture. Second MGOs are voluntary. One isn't born into an MGO as with being born into a nation. MGOs must earn a status of being project worthy. Once an MGO has the requisite year's supply of survival needs they can choose to opt out of any and all projects at any time. This lends every MGO autonomy and sovereignty. This means New Democracy will never attain 100% participation by all humans. Nations that exist today will always exist.

Second, New Democracy mandates only one project to be joined. This project is called project zero. Project zero requires all members to be monitored for MGO member treatment. One can roughly think of this as human rights, yet project zero is not human rights because cultures within MGO will be diametrically opposed, no Utopia. Project zero will ensure MGO members have a life-line to leave any MGO at will if they perceive they are being held against their will.

Further explanation of MGO member management is detailed in subsequent chapters.

New Democracy is anti-ideology in order to be anti-Utopia. This mandates New Democracy have an anti-ideology ideology.

Anti-ideology ideology principles:

Everyone in. Everyone is considered to be in New Democracy no matter their status with an MGO or differing governing organizations.

Indefinite life. Life will go on until the heat death of the universe. Even then, life will work towards preventing the heat death of the universe.

These anti-ideology principles prevent warring between human factions as an anti-ideology principle. The second principle prevents inaction waiting for the End Times. Religion today is sitting on its hands waiting for the second coming. We must prevent that.

Recently there was a book published, "Abundance", that states Utopia as an objective. New Democracy stands in stark contrast. New Democracy supports competing cultures up to the point of war and oppressing people from leaving an MGO. Those are the only limits.

Subtleties of gaslighting and manipulating people to be brain-washed into subjugation are limited to additional project qualifications where project zero is considered the minimal set of requirements. All other projects can prevent trade by seemingly subjugating MGOs.

New Democracy is an experiment. New Democracy has no history. There are no experts on New Democracy. As such New Democracy being adopted is sheer force of will. The question before us all is are we willing?

So, at this point one might be wandering if our current form of government can somehow be salvaged? The answer is no. And the reason for was identified by the Greeks who invented democracy: corruption.

To understand why we need a complete replacement we need to understand that the root cause of all failures of all governments worldwide is corruption. This observation about corruption is not new. Quite simply, absolute power corrupts absolutely. A trait of this observation is that increasing population size increases corruption. Larger population sizes demand more resources, which in turn demands more power.  Power directory correlates to population and corruption. What we are seeing today is nothing more complicated than the worldwide population growth equating to runaway corruption worldwide.

What causes corruption? The Greeks, the Romans and the founders of America all knew answer was hierarchy. None of our ancestors had a working theory for eliminating hierarchy, only the possibility of managing hierarchy. They also know that corruption would eventually overrun this management and predicted this. This is why these days this quote from Jefferson is getting so much attention, "The tree of liberty must be refreshed from time to time with the blood of patriots and tyrants. It is liberty's natural manure." 

Hierarchy doesn't scale. What do I mean by this. The meaning is that as a hierarchy grows it break downs any previous order achieved. As a tree grows it gets healthier. As a hierarchy grows it becomes more corrupt.  Hierarchy's fundamental flaw is that all power and resources are focused on the top of the pyramid for distribution to those below. You know, the pyramid we see on the almighty dollar. The larger the number of people means the more power at the top. The more power equates to more corruption. In Silicon Valley where I worked for decades this is known as your success becomes your failure. This is precisely what happened to the U.S. after WWII. The financial and military success of the U.S. after WWII quickly overran the meager system of checks and balances of the U.S. Constitution. And it wasn't even a fight really. Corruption in the U.S. in 2026 is so large that rewriting the U.S. Constitution wouldn't make a difference. I would posit that the only way to fix the U.S. today would be to split the U.S. into fifty different countries, one for each State. Further we would re-apportion States to have no more than ten million population per State. This would dilute the corruption to something before WWII. We'd also need to eliminate the single U.S. dollar in favor of fifty different dollars, one per new country.

However, re-apportioning the States only kicks the corruption can down the road. Further, it is not just the U.S. where democracy is failing. Democracy is failing worldwide due to the world's increasing population.

Hierarchy is everywhere. Hierarchy defines bureaucracy. Every corporation and every government is built on a bureaucracy that is built on hierarchy. Replacing hierarchy within all of society is a massive undertaking.

The observation that hierarchy doesn't scale means more hierarchy collapses for no other reason than becoming too large. The concept that hierarchy doesn't scale means that hierarchy is less effective every day it grows.

This is why we need the new Mesh design. A mesh has no hierarchy and thus eliminates any system dependent on hierarchy.

* Patriarchy
* Bureaucracy
* Banks
* Corporations
* Nations

New Democracy is an experiment to not only replace governments, but bureaucracy, patriarchy,  and hierarchy. This is how profound it is that New Democracy has no history. There are no experts on New Democracy because mesh organization is completely new. New Democracy being adopted is the sheer force of will to not only replace government, but all bureaucracy.

The question before us all is: are we willing?

